20260529.120523.092 [<ideas.........] ## Core assumptions in the current setup
20260529.120523.693 [<ideas.........] The regression test treats **posterior(train_x)** as one wall-clock number and compares it to **raw FAISS `index.search`**,
20260529.120524.666 [<ideas.........] with a single ratio cap (1.12× at n=512, reference 1.08× from rev 9eaa27). Posterior is assumed to be “FAISS neighbors +
20260529.120525.045 [<ideas.........] small weighted-stats overhead.” Self-search is assumed to be just a batch of n independent queries through `index_search` →
20260529.120525.477 [<ideas.........] `exact_f64_batch_topk`. Tie-break correctness is assumed to require per-row FAISS pool finalization and possible full-row
20260529.120525.849 [<ideas.........] distance scans. CI stability is assumed to come from median-of-10 `perf_counter` samples on ~3 ms operations.
20260529.120526.380 [<ideas.........] Below are three structurally distant explorations within that same formal system (ENN posterior, FAISS index, exact f64
20260529.120526.558 [<ideas.........] tie-break, ratio-based regression). These are boundary ideas, not evaluations.
20260529.120526.607 [<ideas.........] ---
20260529.120527.038 [<ideas.........] ### Idea 1: Self-search as a separate equivalence class (batched distance matrix, zero FAISS in the hot path)
20260529.120527.615 [<ideas.........] **Assumption pushed:** Every query batch, including `x == train_x` with `n_query == n_train`, must go through the generic
20260529.120528.224 [<ideas.........] per-row FAISS → pool-finalize → optional full-row-escalation pipeline in `exact_f64_batch_topk`.
20260529.120528.949 [<ideas.........] **Extreme:** At self-search, all n rows are known at index-build time and the query matrix equals the training matrix. One
20260529.120529.509 [<ideas.........] symmetric `pairwise_sq_l2` call materializes the full n×n distance matrix (already present but hard-disabled via
20260529.120530.043 [<ideas.........] `use_matrix_topk = false` in `neighbor.rs`), then each row’s top-k with tie-break runs against a contiguous slice—no 512
20260529.120530.488 [<ideas.........] FAISS invocations, no per-row `finalize_faiss_pool_topk`, no repeated `row_dist2s_for_query` escalations.
20260529.120530.924 [<ideas.........] **Negation:** Self-search is not “n arbitrary queries”; it is a named regime where the neighbor problem is entirely
20260529.120531.750 [<ideas.........] determined by train_x geometry. Dispatch on `(x.ptr_eq(train_x) && n_query == n_train)` and take a matrix-first path.
20260529.120532.409 [<ideas.........] **Pathological edge:** n=512, d=10 gives ~262k distances—small enough that one BLAS-style pass may beat 512×(FAISS call +
20260529.120533.016 [<ideas.........] Rust/Python boundary + pool bookkeeping). The lattice tie-heavy case (where matrix-topk was disabled) remains on the FAISS
20260529.120533.354 [<ideas.........] path; random continuous data (the failing scenario) does not.
20260529.120533.972 [<ideas.........] **Distance from a tweak:** This is not “raise `faiss_search_k` by 1” or “add one more warmup rep.” It replaces the
20260529.120534.448 [malvin.........] 20260529.120534 Reasoning, sandbox: 173 MiB RSS, 4 procs
20260529.120534.404 [<ideas.........] neighbor-search *representation* for one equivalence class while preserving the same tie-break semantics and posterior stats
20260529.120534.574 [<ideas.........] downstream.
20260529.120534.594 [<ideas.........] ---
20260529.120534.909 [<ideas.........] ### Idea 2: Factorize the regression oracle into a two-link chain (localize the 1.34×)
20260529.120535.718 [<ideas.........] **Assumption pushed:** A single ratio `posterior / faiss` is the right scalar to detect regressions against 9eaa27.
20260529.120535.886 [<ideas.........] **Extreme:** Decompose into two independent caps in the fixture JSON:
20260529.120537.243 [<ideas.........] - `index_neighbor / faiss ≤ β` (neighbor-path overhead: `index_search` vs raw FAISS)
20260529.120537.287 [<ideas.........] - `posterior / index_neighbor ≤ α` (stats + y-gather overhead: `compute_weighted_posterior` only)
20260529.120537.584 [<ideas.........] The current 1.34× conflates both links. **Claim (with evidence from test structure):** `enn_neighbor_distances_and_indices`
20260529.120538.183 [<ideas.........] calls `index.search` directly, while `posterior` calls `get_neighbor_data` → `index_search` → `exact_f64_batch_topk` plus
20260529.120538.487 [<ideas.........] y-neighbor gathering and weighted stats—so a single ratio cannot attribute the 0.9 ms gap.
20260529.120539.029 [<ideas.........] **Negation:** FAISS is not the correct baseline for the *entire* posterior call; it is the baseline for the *index layer
20260529.120539.532 [<ideas.........] only*. The test architecture changes from one inequality to a **chain of accountability** within the same timing harness.
20260529.120540.088 [<ideas.........] **Pathological edge:** A change could make `index_search` 1.25× FAISS while stats stays flat—failing the monolithic test
20260529.120540.697 [<ideas.........] even though the “stats + neighbors” formal decomposition is healthy. Conversely, fixing only stats while index_search
20260529.120540.905 [<ideas.........] regresses would be invisible to a stats-only sub-test.
20260529.120541.373 [<ideas.........] **Distance from a tweak:** Not loosening `max_ratio` from 1.12 to 1.35. The test’s *shape* changes: two assertions, two
20260529.120541.585 [<ideas.........] fixture thresholds, same scenarios and seeds.
20260529.120541.639 [<ideas.........] ---
20260529.120541.932 [<ideas.........] ### Idea 3: Replace wall-clock ratio with a committed work ledger (negate timing as the CI signal)
20260529.120542.470 [<ideas.........] **Assumption pushed:** Median wall-clock on ~3 ms operations (`t_post≈0.0035s`, `t_faiss≈0.0026s` per failure logs) is
20260529.120542.695 [<ideas.........] stable enough to enforce a 4% margin (1.12 vs 1.08).
20260529.120543.421 [<ideas.........] **Extreme:** At n=512 both arms finish in a few milliseconds; a 0.9 ms absolute gap is ~34% relative—well inside single-run
20260529.120543.763 [<ideas.........] jitter on shared CI runners. Push timing to its asymptotic uselessness: when both operands are noise-dominated, **any**
20260529.120544.106 [<ideas.........] ratio threshold becomes a coin flip.
20260529.120544.643 [<ideas.........] **Negation:** Do not measure how fast the VM runs; measure how much *work the formal algorithm does*. Add a `#[cfg(test)]`
20260529.120545.394 [<ideas.........] (or feature-gated) ledger in the Rust posterior path counting: FAISS `search` calls, full-row distance scans
20260529.120545.558 [<ideas.........] (`row_dist2s_for_query`), `dist2s_for_neighbor_indices` recomputations, heap allocations. Commit per-scenario ceilings in
20260529.120545.763 [<ideas.........] `posterior_speed_baseline.json` alongside (or instead of) `max_ratio`.
20260529.120546.273 [<ideas.........] **Pathological edge:** A refactor that caches row distances across queries could pass wall-clock while violating a “no more
20260529.120546.950 [<ideas.........] than one full n-scan per query” invariant from 9eaa27—or fail wall-clock on a slow runner while doing identical work.
20260529.120547.267 [<ideas.........] Op-count is immune to CPU frequency and co-tenant noise.
20260529.120548.028 [<ideas.........] **Distance from a tweak:** Not “increase reps from 10 to 50” or “pin to a performance core.” The pass/fail predicate changes
20260529.120548.183 [<ideas.........] category: from duration ratio to monotonic work budget, still tied to the same formal neighbor+stats pipeline.
20260529.120548.222 [<ideas.........] ---
20260529.120548.278 [<ideas.........] ## tl;dr
20260529.120548.819 [<ideas.........] Three boundary moves within the same ENN/FAISS/tie-break system: (1) treat self-search as its own regime and serve neighbors
20260529.120549.414 [<ideas.........] from one batched distance matrix instead of 512 FAISS round-trips; (2) split the failing single ratio into
20260529.120549.952 [<ideas.........] `index_search/faiss` and `posterior/index_search` so the 1.34× localizes; (3) gate CI on a committed Rust work ledger
20260529.120550.555 [<ideas.........] (distance evals, scans, allocs) instead of millisecond wall-clock that is mostly noise at n=512.
